# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Variational Quantum Deflation (VQD) {#variational-quantum-deflation-vqd}"
msgstr "الانحراف الكمي التبايُني (VQD) {#variational-quantum-deflation-vqd}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[VQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.08138) is an iterative method that extends VQE to obtain the first $k$ eigenvalues of an observable $\\hat{H}$ with eigenvalues $\\{\\lambda_0, \\lambda_1,...,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$, where $N\\geq k$, instead of only the first. For the rest of this section, we will assume, without loss of generality, that $\\lambda_0\\leq\\lambda_1\\leq...\\leq\\lambda_{N-1}$. VQD introduces the notion of a penalty cost to guide the optimization process.\n"
msgstr "[VQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.08138) هو أسلوب تكراري يمتد على VQE للحصول على أول $k$ قيم ذاتية للمؤثر القابل للرصد $\\hat{H}$ ذات قيم ذاتية $\\{\\lambda_0, \\lambda_1,...,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$، حيث $N\\geq k$، بدلًا من الحصول على الأولى فقط. في بقية هذا القسم، سنفترض دون فقدان العمومية أن $\\lambda_0\\leq\\lambda_1\\leq...\\leq\\lambda_{N-1}$. يُدخل VQD مفهوم تكلفة العقوبة لتوجيه عملية التحسين.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A diagram showing how VQD uses the components of a variational algorithm.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/instances-and-extensions/instances-vqd.svg)\n"
"VQD introduces a penalty term, denoted as $\\beta$, to balance the contribution of each overlap term to the cost. This penalty term serves to penalize the optimization process if orthogonality is not achieved. We impose this constraint because the eigenstates of an observable, or a Hermitian operator, corresponding to different eigenvalues are always mutually orthogonal, or can be made to be so in the case of degeneracy or repeated eigenvalues. Thus, by enforcing orthogonality with the eigenstate corresponding to $\\lambda_0$, we are effectively optimizing over the subspace that corresponds to the rest of the eigenvalues $\\{\\lambda_1, \\lambda_2,..., \\lambda_{N-1}\\}$. Here, $\\lambda_1$ is the lowest eigenvalue from the rest of the eigenvalues and, therefore, the optimal solution of the new problem can be obtained using the variational theorem.\n"
msgstr ""
"![A diagram showing how VQD uses the components of a variational algorithm.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/instances-and-extensions/instances-vqd.svg)\n"
"VQD introduces a penalty term, denoted as $\\beta$, to balance the contribution of each overlap term to the cost. This penalty term serves to penalize the optimization process if orthogonality is not achieved. We impose this constraint because the eigenstates of an observable, or a Hermitian operator, corresponding to different eigenvalues are always mutually orthogonal, or can be made to be so in the case of degeneracy or repeated eigenvalues. Thus, by enforcing orthogonality with the eigenstate corresponding to $\\lambda_0$, we are effectively optimizing over the subspace that corresponds to the rest of the eigenvalues $\\{\\lambda_1, \\lambda_2,..., \\lambda_{N-1}\\}$. Here, $\\lambda_1$ is the lowest eigenvalue from the rest of the eigenvalues and, therefore, the optimal solution of the new problem can be obtained using the variational theorem.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The general idea behind VQD is to use VQE as usual to obtain the lowest eigenvalue $\\lambda_0 := C_0(\\vec\\theta^0) \\equiv C_\\text{VQE}(\\vec\\theta^0)$ along with the corresponding (approximate) eigenstate $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle$ for some optimal parameter vector $\\vec{\\theta^0}$. Then, to obtain the next eigenvalue $\\lambda_1 > \\lambda_0$, instead of minimizing the cost function $C_0(\\vec{\\theta}) := \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle$, we optimize:\n"
msgstr "يُدخل VQD حدًّا للعقوبة يُرمز له بـ $\\beta$، لموازنة إسهام كل حد تداخل في التكلفة. يُعاقب هذا الحد عملية التحسين إذا لم يتحقق التعامد. نفرض هذا القيد لأن الحالات الذاتية لمؤثر قابل للرصد، أو مؤثر هيرميتي، المقابلة لقيم ذاتية مختلفة تكون دائمًا متعامدة بالتبادل، أو يمكن جعلها كذلك في حالة التعدد أو تكرار القيم الذاتية. وبالتالي، بفرض التعامد مع الحالة الذاتية المقابلة لـ $\\lambda_0$، نُحسِّن فعليًا في الفضاء الجزئي المقابل لبقية القيم الذاتية $\\{\\lambda_1, \\lambda_2,..., \\lambda_{N-1}\\}$. هنا، $\\lambda_1$ هي أصغر قيمة ذاتية من بقية القيم الذاتية، وبالتالي يمكن الحصول على الحل الأمثل للمسألة الجديدة باستخدام المبرهنة التبايُنية.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"C_1(\\vec{\\theta}) :=\n"
"C_0(\\vec{\\theta})+ \\beta_0 |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle  |^2\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"C_1(\\vec{\\theta}) :=\n"
"C_0(\\vec{\\theta})+ \\beta_0 |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle  |^2\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: emptied 2026-09-05, previous translation failed check.py
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The positive value $\\beta_0$ should ideally be greater than $\\lambda_1-\\lambda_0$.\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: emptied 2026-09-05, previous translation failed check.py
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This introduces a new cost function that can be viewed as a constrained problem, where we minimize $C_\\text{VQE}(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle$ subject to the constraint that the state must be orthogonal to the previously obtained $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle$, with $\\beta_0$ acting as a penalty term if the constraint is not satisfied.\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: emptied 2026-09-05, previous translation failed check.py
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Alternatively, this new problem can be interpreted as running VQE on the new observable:\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H_1} := \\hat{H} + \\beta_0 |\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})|\n"
"\\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad\n"
"C_1(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H_1} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H_1} := \\hat{H} + \\beta_0 |\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})|\n"
"\\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad\n"
"C_1(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H_1} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: emptied 2026-09-05, previous translation failed check.py
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Assuming that the solution to the new problem is $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle$, the expected value of $\\hat{H}$ (not $\\hat{H_1}$) should be $ \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle = \\lambda_1$.\n"
"To obtain the third eigenvalue $\\lambda_2$, the cost function to optimize is:\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"C_2(\\vec{\\theta}) :=\n"
"C_1(\\vec{\\theta}) + \\beta_1 |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle  |^2\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"C_2(\\vec{\\theta}) :=\n"
"C_1(\\vec{\\theta}) + \\beta_1 |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle  |^2\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: emptied 2026-09-05, previous translation failed check.py
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $\\beta_1$ is a positive constant large enough to enforce orthogonality of the solution state to both $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle$ and $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle$. This penalizes states in the search space that do not meet this requirement, effectively restricting the search space. Thus, the optimal solution of the new problem should be the eigenstate corresponding to $\\lambda_2$.\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: emptied 2026-09-05, previous translation failed check.py
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Like the previous case, this new problem can also be interpreted as VQE with the observable:\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H_2} := \\hat{H_1} + \\beta_1 |\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})|\n"
"\\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad\n"
"C_2(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H_2} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H_2} := \\hat{H_1} + \\beta_1 |\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})|\n"
"\\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad\n"
"C_2(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H_2} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: emptied 2026-09-05, previous translation failed check.py
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the solution to this new problem is $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^2})\\rangle$, the expected value of $\\hat{H}$ (not $\\hat{H_2}$) should be $ \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^2}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^2})\\rangle = \\lambda_2$.\n"
"Analogously, to obtain the $k$-th eigenvalue $\\lambda_{k-1}$, you would minimize the cost function:\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"C_{k-1}(\\vec{\\theta}) :=\n"
"C_{k-2}(\\vec{\\theta}) + \\beta_{k-2} |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^{k-2}})\\rangle  |^2,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"C_{k-1}(\\vec{\\theta}) :=\n"
"C_{k-2}(\\vec{\\theta}) + \\beta_{k-2} |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^{k-2}})\\rangle  |^2,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Remember that we defined $\\vec{\\theta^j}$ such that $\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle = \\lambda_j, \\forall j<k$. This problem is equivalent to minimizing $C(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle$ but with the constraint that the state must be orthogonal to $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle ; \\forall j \\in {0, \\cdots, k-1}$, thereby restricting the search space to the subspace corresponding to the eigenvalues $\\{\\lambda_{k-1},\\cdots,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$.\n"
msgstr "إذا كان حل هذه المسألة الجديدة هو $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^2})\\rangle$، يجب أن تكون القيمة المتوقعة لـ $\\hat{H}$ (وليس $\\hat{H_2}$) هي $ \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^2}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^2})\\rangle = \\lambda_2$.\n"

# doq: emptied 2026-09-05, previous translation failed check.py
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This problem is equivalent to a VQE with the observable:\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H}_{k-1} :=\n"
"\\hat{H}_{k-2} + \\beta_{k-2} |\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^{k-2}})\\rangle \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^{k-2}})|\n"
"\\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad\n"
"C_{k-1}(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H}_{k-1} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H}_{k-1} :=\n"
"\\hat{H}_{k-2} + \\beta_{k-2} |\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^{k-2}})\\rangle \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^{k-2}})|\n"
"\\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad\n"
"C_{k-1}(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H}_{k-1} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: emptied 2026-09-05, previous translation failed check.py
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As you can see from the process, to obtain the $k$-th eigenvalue, you need the (approximate) eigenstates of the previous $k-1$ eigenvalues, so you would need to run VQE a total of $k$ times. Therefore, VQD's cost function is as follows:\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"C_k(\\vec{\\theta}) =\n"
"\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle +\n"
"\\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}\\beta_j |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle |^2\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"C_k(\\vec{\\theta}) =\n"
"\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle +\n"
"\\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}\\beta_j |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle |^2\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Theoretical layout {#theoretical-layout-2}"
